 "script": "Daylight saving time ended in Europe this weekend. US clocks fall back November 1, ABC News reports. This week, New York is only four hours behind London. Europe's Parliament voted to scrap the switch in 2019, but EU governments never agreed. In July, the US House voted to make daylight saving time permanent. The vote was 308 to 117. President Trump backs it, but the bill has stalled in the Senate. Until Congress acts, clocks keep changing. Which would you keep all year? Lighter mornings or lighter evenings? Tell us below.",
